      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $3|2x-5|+13=4,$ then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3|2x-5|+13 & =4 \\\\ 3|2x-5| & =-9 \\\\ |2x-5| & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the right-hand side is negative. Therefore, the equation has no solutions.",
